            ⛰️ Moderate Hikes
          </a>
          <a href="#daytrips" class="px-4 py-2 bg-cyan-50 text-cyan-700 rounded-lg hover:bg-cyan-100 transition-colors font-medium text-sm">
            🚗 Farther Day Trips
          </a>
          <a href="#all" class="px-4 py-2 bg-purple-50 text-purple-700 rounded-lg hover:bg-purple-100 transition-colors font-medium text-sm">
            📍 All {nearbyHikes.length} Trails
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Intro Content -->
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-16 bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm border border-stone-200">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4">New Haven Reaches Both Connecticut's Hills and New York's Hudson Highlands</h2>

        <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
          New Haven sits on the coast, so its own city parkland is flat by comparison to what's inland.
          Drive 45 to 75 minutes northwest on Route 8 or the Merritt Parkway and you reach the same
          Litchfield Hills cluster that serves Hartford — real forested ridgelines, including Bear
          Mountain, Connecticut's own highest summit near Salisbury. What New Haven has that Hartford
          doesn't: a straight shot down I-95 and I-84 to New York's Hudson Highlands, where Bear Mountain
          State Park, Storm King and Breakneck Ridge overlook the Hudson River — some of the most iconic
          day hikes in the Northeast, and genuinely closer to New Haven than they are to most of inland
          Connecticut.
        </p>

        <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
          This guide covers all {nearbyHikes.length} trails within 100 miles of New Haven, sorted by actual
          distance from real trailhead coordinates — not the city center. Each trail includes:
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
          <li>✓ <strong>Exact distance from New Haven</strong> (measured from the trailhead, not the summit)</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Trail difficulty rating</strong> (easy, moderate, hard)</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Elevation gain & distance</strong></li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Parking information & fees</strong></li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Interactive trail maps</strong></li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Real-time weather conditions</strong></li>
