              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-600 transform transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="p-4 text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
              Bear Mountain State Park, Storm King and Breakneck Ridge in New York's Hudson Highlands are roughly 55 miles
              from New Haven — about a 75-minute drive via I-84 and the Taconic State Parkway. New Haven's position on
              I-95 and the Merritt Parkway puts this cluster within easier day-trip range than it is from Hartford.
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Hiking Tips for New Haven Area -->
      <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-50 to-blue-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-emerald-200">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-6">Essential Tips for Hiking Near New Haven</h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">🚗</span> Getting There
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• For the Litchfield Hills, take Route 8 N or the Merritt Parkway to Route 118/126</li>
              <li>• For Bear Mountain, Connecticut's own high summit, continue north on US-7</li>
              <li>• For New York's Hudson Highlands, take I-95 S to I-287 W, then the Taconic State Pkwy</li>
              <li>• Download offline maps in case of poor cell service on back roads</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">🎒</span> What to Bring
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• Water: 2+ liters per person</li>
              <li>• Snacks: Trail mix, energy bars, fruit</li>
              <li>• Layers: New England and Hudson Valley weather shifts fast</li>
              <li>• First aid kit & headlamp</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">📅</span> Best Times to Visit
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
